  "publicationInference": {
    "supported": "The outstanding Escape transition can satisfy later clickWorld frame/scene floors while the newly selected inspector is still unpublished. The displayed empty Page inspector spans the source-click state snapshot, and the selected Rectangle inspector appears after the inspector click. A scalar scene counter does not identify the layout generation belonging to a control.",
    "sourceSupport": [
      "samples/FerroDesign/tests/matching-browser.mjs:48\u201356: selectSource presses Escape and waits only exact empty selection before clickWorld.",
      "samples/FerroDesign/tests/browser.mjs:228\u2013244: clickWorld captures current frame/scene counters immediately before its selecting click; it waits only larger counters after selection changes.",
      "samples/FerroDesign/crates/ferrodesign-app/src/shell.rs:145\u2013157: sceneFrames counts public renderer.scene_invalidated notifications;659\u2013670 exposes current layout/visibility, not hit-test readback.",
      "src/FerroUI.Base/rendering/composition/compositing_renderer.rs:293\u2013313: only one scene-invalidated completion callback is queued; it is posted at INPUT after commit.rendered(), so a prior outstanding completion may satisfy a later scalar counter threshold.",
      "src/FerroUI.Base/rendering/composition/server/server_compositor.rs:739\u2013770: targets render before visual_readback_update_pass; the completed notification follows those operations.",
      "samples/FerroDesign/crates/ferrodesign-app/src/shell.rs:440,1860 and shell/selection.rs:7\u201328: the button dispatches select-matching; after draft validation the handler shows ModalBackdrop and builds named row controls synchronously."
    ],
    "notProven": [
      "The trace does not expose the actual native hit-test target, pointer-capture owner, button Click event, or callback invocation. It therefore cannot prove the exact event-consumption path or exclude every application guard.",
      "Screencast frameSwapWallTime is a presentation timestamp, not a native per-control hit-test generation. Pixel timing corroborates the boundary but is not itself an input-hit query.",
      "The frame+scene counters are coalesced and cannot prove per-target readiness; adding another unconditional idle scene wait could deadlock a quiescent canvas.",
      "This diagnosis does not claim high memory caused this failure."
    ]
  },
  "publicApiCondition": {
    "availableInCurrentBrowserBridge": false,
    "description": "At the exact center coordinate that JavaScript will click, query the full native input root and accept only a returned input element identical to the intended control or a visual descendant of it, while retaining the existing valid-layout/visible/enabled checks.",
    "nativePath": "control.get_input_root().root_element(); translate the EditorRoot-space click point using self.root.translate_point(point, &input_root); input_root.input_hit_test(translated); require hit identity==target OR target.is_visual_ancestor_of(hit).",
    "reasonForFullRoot": "The full root query includes current clipping and occluding siblings; hit testing only the target subtree would incorrectly bypass blockers.",
    "source": "visual_extensions.rs:461,471,538; input_extensions.rs:65,338; composition/compositing_renderer.rs:232; composition/composition_target.rs:304.",
    "limitations": "This samples current uncaptured native hit-test readiness. MouseDevice::mouse_down chooses existing pointer capture first. It does not guarantee future delivery, immutable scene state, pointer release/click activation, or command success. Preserve a single real pointer click and exact modal-open/command outcome afterward; do not invoke commands or force rendering."
  },
  "proposedTestOnlyCorrection": {
    "scope": "Only matching-browser.mjs; parent authorized separate agent to prepare this correction. Original f2bb files remain unchanged in the preserved harness.",
    "beforeSourceSelection": "Capture native state before Escape; when selection is actually cleared, require exact empty selection and the corresponding native frame and scene progression before issuing the next selecting canvas click. Retain clickWorld publication checks for that subsequent transition.",
    "afterInspectorClick": "Require exact ModalBackdrop-visible and intended named row visibility/validity before the one row click, with the existing finite10000ms deadline. Preserve existing exact selected IDs, modal closure, document, history, redo and revision assertions.",
    "verificationNeeded": "One bounded both-mode matching run on a separately copied, published corrected harness; no automatic full rerun or application rebuild."
  },
